<div class="page-heading wrap"><p class="eyebrow">GETTING STARTED / <%= h(config.fetch('release')) %></p><h1>From a Grape API<br>to OpenAPI.</h1><p class="intro">Install the gem, describe an endpoint, and generate your first specification.</p></div>
<div class="guide-layout wrap">
  <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#install">01 / Install</a><a href="#define">02 / Define your API</a><a href="#serve">03 / Serve the document</a><a href="#generate">04 / Generate directly</a><a href="#integrations">05 / Add integrations</a><a href="#reference">Reference docs ↗</a></nav>
  <article class="guide-content">
    <section id="install"><p class="step">01 / INSTALL</p><h2>Add grape-oas</h2><p>Use Ruby 3.2 or newer and Grape 3.0 or newer. Add the gem to your application’s Gemfile:</p><%= code('gem "grape-oas"') %><p>Then install your dependencies:</p><%= code('bundle install') %></section>
    <section id="define"><p class="step">02 / DEFINE YOUR API</p><h2>A small, working example</h2><p>This API documents an integer path parameter and exposes a specification at <code>/swagger_doc</code>.</p><%= code(@example) %><p>Mount <code>CatalogAPI</code> in your Rack application as you would any Grape API.</p></section>
    <section id="serve"><p class="step">03 / SERVE THE DOCUMENT</p><h2>Choose your OpenAPI format</h2><p><code>add_oas_documentation</code> serves JSON and excludes documentation routes from the specification by default.</p><div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Documentation endpoints" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Endpoint</th><th scope="col">Format</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>/swagger_doc</code></td><td>OpenAPI 3.0, the default</td></tr><tr><td><code>/swagger_doc?oas=2</code></td><td>OpenAPI 2.0</td></tr><tr><td><code>/swagger_doc?oas=3.1</code></td><td>OpenAPI 3.1</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
    <section id="generate"><p class="step">04 / GENERATE DIRECTLY</p><h2>Export without an endpoint</h2><p>With your API loaded, generate a Ruby hash and serialize it to JSON:</p><%= code("require \"json\"\n\nspec = GrapeOAS.generate(app: CatalogAPI, schema_type: :oas31)\nFile.write(\"openapi.json\", JSON.pretty_generate(spec))") %><p>Use <code>:oas2</code>, <code>:oas3</code>, or <code>:oas31</code> to choose the format. <a href="<%= docs('docs/USAGE.md') %>">Explore more usage examples ↗</a></p></section>
    <section id="integrations"><p class="step">05 / ADD INTEGRATIONS</p><h2>Bring your schemas along</h2><p>Install the integrations your application uses. They are optional dependencies:</p><%= code("gem \"grape-entity\"    # Response entities\ngem \"dry-validation\"  # Validation contracts\ngem \"dry-schema\"      # Standalone schemas") %><p><a href="<%= docs('docs/INTROSPECTORS.md') %>">Read about schema introspection ↗</a></p></section>
    <section id="reference"><p class="step">KEEP GOING</p><h2>The details live in the reference</h2><div class="reference-links"><a href="<%= docs('docs/CONFIGURATION.md') %>">Configuration <span>↗</span></a><a href="<%= docs('docs/USAGE.md') %>">Usage and examples <span>↗</span></a><a href="<%= docs('docs/EXPORTERS.md') %>">Custom exporters <span>↗</span></a><a href="<%= docs('UPGRADING.md') %>">Upgrading <span>↗</span></a></div><p>These links point to the current repository docs, which may include changes newer than this guide’s release.</p></section>
  </article>
</div>
